{
  "evidence": "A (first text – Reform UK): Freeze non‑essential immigration; detain and rapidly remove arrivals; leave the ECHR; increase stop and search and tougher penalties; recruit 40,000 police; restrict gender‑related practices in schools; replace Equalities Act/DEI rules; Free Speech Bill; scrap Net Zero and expand domestic oil and gas; cut foreign aid; two‑strike rule on job offers and stricter benefit assessments; eliminate NHS waiting lists with vouchers and private capacity; broad tax cuts (higher personal thresholds, fuel duty cut, inheritance tax changes).\nB (second text – Lib Dem proposals): Right to see a GP in 7 days; +8,000 GPs; NHS dentistry access; mental health hubs; free personal care; Carer’s Minimum Wage; abolish two‑child limit and benefit cap; free school meals for children in poverty; disability benefit reform; strong climate plan (net zero 2045, 90% renewables by 2030, home upgrades, social energy tariff); sewage and nature recovery measures; build 380,000 homes/year incl. 150,000 social; end no‑fault evictions; worker protections and fairer status for freelancers; tax fairness (windfall tax, CGT reform, higher Digital Services Tax, levy on buybacks); uphold Human Rights Act/ECHR; more compassionate, rules‑based asylum with faster decisions and right to work; community policing and justice backlog reduction; increase defence spending towards 2.5% GDP.",
  "reasoning": "Because the electorate’s top priorities are Care, Equality and Proportionality, B aligns better by centering social care and health access, poverty reduction, fairer taxation and worker protections, and environmental stewardship, while A emphasizes immigration crackdowns, tax cuts tilted away from equality, and scrapping Net Zero. With only moderate weight on Loyalty/Authority and low on Sanctity, A’s focus on ECHR exit, hardline policing, and cultural restrictions over-indexes those foundations, whereas B balances some policing/defence with stronger commitments to welfare and rights that map more closely to the profile.",
  "confidence": "high",
  "winner": "B"
}
